        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: block mixed-case cron shell jobs from agent tool [AI]",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where agent-created cron jobs could bypass the agent cron tool's shell-execution restriction when cron kind values used alternate casing.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe agent cron tool now applies the same case-insensitive kind interpretation used by cron normalization when enforcing its shell-execution deny rule. CLI and Gateway cron command support are unchanged; this only tightens the agent-tool boundary before dispatching `cron.add` or `cron.update`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgent tool calls can no longer create or edit command-backed cron jobs through mixed-case payload or schedule kinds. Normal agent-turn and system-event cron jobs continue to work through the existing cron tool flow.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAI-assisted.\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/cron-tool.test.ts` passed: 1 file, 144 tests.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Remote Testbox/AWS Crabbox proof was unavailable in this environment before source sync: installed Crabbox is 0.20.0 for Testbox, and the AWS broker is not logged in on this host.\n",
